# Line endings.
#
# The deploy scripts are checked out on a Linux VM and executed there. A CRLF line ending on
# the shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter called "/usr/bin/env bash\r", which
# fails with the famously unhelpful "bad interpreter: No such file or directory". Forcing LF
# on everything the VM runs removes a whole afternoon of confusion.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
